{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.492,
   "text": "On a road trip out west, we stopped at a canyon overlook called Echo Point."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.092,
   "end": 14.02,
   "text": "A rusted sign on the railing had one rule. Never shout your own name."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 15.02,
   "end": 20.631,
   "text": "My little brother Danny laughed, cupped his hands... and yelled his name as loud as he could."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 21.431,
   "end": 25.143,
   "text": "The canyon threw it back. Danny... Danny... Danny..."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 26.543,
   "end": 30.66,
   "text": "Then it just kept going. Long after any echo should have stopped."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 32.26,
   "end": 37.508,
   "text": "That night, at a motel off the highway, I woke up to a whisper outside our door."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 38.308,
   "end": 39.78,
   "text": "Danny... Danny..."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 41.38,
   "end": 46.073,
   "text": "Mom and Dad didn't stir. Danny was asleep in the bed next to mine."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 46.873,
   "end": 51.268,
   "text": "The whisper slid closer... right up to the crack under the door."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 52.668,
   "end": 56.636,
   "text": "And then, in the dark... Danny sat up and answered. I'm here."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 58.636,
   "end": 63.351,
   "text": "In the morning, he seemed fine. Just quiet. Smiling a little too much."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 64.351,
   "end": 68.447,
   "text": "But today at breakfast, he leaned across the table and asked me..."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 69.847,
   "end": 71.66,
   "text": "What's your name again?"
  }
 ],
